  "notes": "Digitized from the Kodak E-4021 datasheet of September 2008. Kodak calls it \"a low contrast paper, making it an ideal choice for portrait, studio, and wedding photography\"; the 2009 edition says it \"was discontinued in late 2006\". The sheet prints one spectral sensitivity and one dye density plot for PORTRA ENDURA and SUPRA ENDURA together; both profiles carry them. Status A curves for a 0.5 s sensitometric exposure; the sheet does not say what light the sensitometer used, so the enlarger here is the same stand-in as ENDURA Premier's. No granularity and no MTF on the sheet. R and G end at the same density; R is the curve above at log H -0.9, where the sheet prints its R label, and B the lowest, by the label printed below its end. The frame's bottom edge sits 0.022 D above the ticks' zero and its right edge 0.017 log H short of the ticks' 0.0; the tick reading is kept, as for Portra 160's sheet, so the densities carry plus or minus 0.02 D.",
